      "Entropic Uprising": {"route":"spells","pace":"COMBAT INTO CASCADE","complexity":"Advanced","theme":"Yidris turns a successful combat hit into cascade for spells you cast from your hand that turn.","plan":"Fix all four colors, connect with Yidris and cast from hand in your second main phase to collect cascade value.","mulligan":"Keep three lands with several colors, a fixing spell and an early play.","tip":"Yidris must deal combat damage to a player first. The cascade grant applies to later hand casts that turn.","keys":["Bloodbraid Elf","Whispering Madness","Cruel Entertainment"]},
      "Open Hostility": {"route":"bigCreatures","pace":"FOUR-COLOR AGGRESSION","complexity":"Intermediate","theme":"Saskia chooses a player as she enters and sends extra creature damage toward that player.","plan":"Fix your colors, build an attacking board and choose the player you want to pressure through attacks on the rest of the table.","mulligan":"Keep three lands, fixing and two early creatures.","tip":"Saskia’s extra damage is dealt by the original creature and is not combat damage. The chosen player may also be the original defender.","keys":["Brutal Hordechief","Tymna the Weaver","Crackling Doom"]},
      "Stalwart Unity": {"route":"politics","pace":"SHARED RESOURCES AND DEFENSE","complexity":"Advanced","theme":"Kynaios and Tiro help every player develop while your defenses buy time to use the extra resources.","plan":"Fix your colors, encourage development and protect yourself with taxes and selective removal before committing finishers.","mulligan":"Keep three lands, color fixing and a defensive or draw engine.","tip":"You always draw first at your end step. Each opponent who declines to put a land onto the battlefield draws afterward.","keys":["Rites of Flourishing","Sphere of Safety","Reverse the Sands"]},
      "Breed Lethality": {"route":"counters","pace":"COUNTERS AND PROLIFERATE","complexity":"Intermediate","theme":"Atraxa proliferates at your end step while the deck spreads counters across an expanding board.","plan":"Fix four colors, put counters on useful creatures and protect your board so each end step adds lasting growth.","mulligan":"Keep three lands, early fixing and a creature or engine that starts with counters.","tip":"Proliferate adds one counter of each kind already present on each chosen permanent or player. Choose carefully.","keys":["Reyhan, Last of the Abzan","Corpsejack Menace","Deepglow Skate"]},
      "Invent Superiority": {"route":"artifacts","pace":"ARTIFACT SACRIFICE AND REUSE","complexity":"Advanced","theme":"Breya makes Thopters and converts spare artifacts into damage, removal or life.","plan":"Develop artifact mana, protect your useful machines and recycle expendable artifacts into Breya activations or graveyard returns.","mulligan":"Keep three lands, a mana artifact and an inexpensive artifact or recursion spell.","tip":"Breya’s ability costs two mana and two artifacts. Tokens can pay the sacrifice cost, and Breya can sacrifice herself.","keys":["Silas Renn, Seeker Adept","Daretti, Scrap Savant","Open the Vaults"]},
    "Forged in Stone": {"route":"artifacts","pace":"EQUIPMENT MIDRANGE","complexity":"Intermediate","theme":"Nahiri forges Equipment, raises Kor Soldiers, and rebuilds a resilient white army.","plan":"Develop mana and Equipment, then use Nahiri to create defenders and recover your strongest relics. Protect loyalty with a growing army and finish with an equipped threat.","mulligan":"Keep three lands, an early mana rock, and a creature or Equipment.","tip":"Nahiri can put an Equipment from either hand or graveyard onto the battlefield. Her first ability can attach Equipment without paying its equip cost.","keys":["Kemba, Kha Regent","Sun Titan","Skullclamp"]},
